<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19528" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gēryon</span></b> ,
		ōnis, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gēryŏnēs</span></b> ,
			ae (cf. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 9, § 90</span></i>
		Müll.; archaic <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen. sing.</i>, Geryonaī, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
				28</span></i>.—<i>Abl.</i> scanned
			Gērȳŏne, <i><span class="en">Sid.
				Carm. 13, 13</span></i>), m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γηρυών</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γηρυόνης</span>, <i>a mythic king in Spain having
				three bodies</i>, <i>whose oxen were carried off
				by Hercules</i>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				662</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 202</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 9,
			92</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 2, 14, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 13,
				201</span></i>; Hyg. Fab. praef. <i>fin.—Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in hac (Erythia insula) Geryones habitasse a
					quibusdam existimantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 22, 36, § 120</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Geryonis oraculum,</span>”
				<i>at Patavium</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 14</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gēryŏ-nācĕus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Geryonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genere Geryonaceo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Aul. 3, 6, 18</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gē-ryŏnēus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Geryonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
